flowchart TB
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: where is each event of budget execution recorded, by which unit, and from which records are the reports built?
  %% IDEA: an agency keeps two sets of records for the same money. The BUDGET REGISTRIES follow legal authority (appropriation, allotment, obligation, disbursement). They are lists with running balances, not double-entry books. The ACCOUNTING BOOKS follow assets, liabilities, revenue and expenses by double entry on the accrual basis. An obligation appears only in the registries. A journal entry is made only when a delivery is accepted or cash moves.
  %% READING: top row = source documents. Blue = records of the budget unit. Green = records of the accounting unit. Yellow = reports.
  %% SOURCES: registries RAPAL, RAOD and RBUD as sources of the accountability reports, FAR reports by fund cluster [JC2019-1]. Obligations are not journalized, entries for NCA receipt and for payment [GAM-GUIDE]. Government Accounting Manual in three volumes, based on Philippine Public Sector Accounting Standards, Volume III = Revised Chart of Accounts [COA2015-007]. Object code of UACS = account code of the Revised Chart of Accounts plus sub-object [JC2017-1]. Statements sent to COA through the AFR System [COA-GAS]. Reports through URS [NBC599][JC2019-1].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: the names of the four journals and of the financial statements, the registry of revenue, the trial balance step, consolidation by the central office, the ORS number as a field of the voucher (on the payment order it is verified [LDDAP-FORM]). Check Government Accounting Manual Volume II for the exact forms.

  S1["GAA, SARO, GARO,<br/>sub-allotment advice"]:::src
  S2["Obligation Request<br/>and Status (ORS)"]:::src
  S3["Disbursement voucher, payroll,<br/>LDDAP-ADA, check"]:::src
  S4["Official receipts,<br/>deposit slips"]:::src
  S5["Inspection and acceptance report,<br/>liquidation report, other documents"]:::src

  subgraph BUD["BUDGET UNIT: REGISTRIES (single entry, by fund cluster)"]
    R1["RAPAL<br/>Registry of Appropriations<br/>and Allotments"]
    R2["RAOD<br/>Registries of Allotments, Obligations<br/>and Disbursements, one per expense class"]
    R3["RBUD<br/>Registries of Budget, Utilization and<br/>Disbursements, for off-budget funds"]
    R4["Registry of revenue<br/>and other receipts"]
  end

  subgraph ACC["ACCOUNTING UNIT: BOOKS (double entry, accrual, by fund cluster)"]
    J0["Journal Entry Voucher (JEV)<br/>one per transaction, with account codes<br/>from the Revised Chart of Accounts"]
    J1["Journals<br/>general, cash receipts, cash disbursements,<br/>check disbursements"]
    J2["General ledger and<br/>subsidiary ledgers"]
    J3["Trial balance<br/>monthly, quarterly, year-end"]
  end

  O1["Budget and Financial Accountability Reports (BFARs)<br/>FAR 1 to FAR 6 and BAR 1, through URS"]:::out
  O2["Financial statements<br/>financial position, financial performance,<br/>changes in net assets, cash flows,<br/>comparison of budget and actual amounts, notes"]:::out

  S1 --> R1
  R1 --> R2
  S2 --> R2
  S3 --> R2
  S3 --> R3
  S4 --> R4
  S3 --> J0
  S4 --> J0
  S5 --> J0
  J0 --> J1 --> J2 --> J3
  R1 --> O1
  R2 --> O1
  R3 --> O1
  R4 --> O1
  J3 --> O2
  R2 -. "budget figures" .-> O2

  NOTE["THE LINK BETWEEN THE TWO SETS IS THE CODE: the object code in a registry line and the account code<br/>in a journal entry come from the same Revised Chart of Accounts (the object segment of UACS).<br/>THE LINK BETWEEN TWO RECORDS OF ONE TRANSACTION IS A DOCUMENT NUMBER:<br/>the ORS number is written on the voucher and on the payment order."]
  O1 ~~~ NOTE
  O2 ~~~ NOTE

